@startuml
title Dataspace Protocol (DSP 2025-1) — Catalog, Contract Negotiation & Transfer (dsp-rs)
autonumber
skinparam Style strictuml
skinparam SequenceMessageAlignment center
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FEF9E7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #D4AC0D

actor "Data Consumer\n(internal API caller)" as User
participant "Consumer Connector\n(did:web:party-b-connector%3A3000)\nhttp://party-b-connector:3000" as Consumer
participant "Consumer Wallet\n(SSI / OpenID4VP)" as Wallet
participant "Provider Connector\n(did:web:party-a-connector%3A3000)\nhttp://party-a-connector:3000" as Provider

note over Consumer, Provider #EBF5FB
  All DSP messages are exchanged under the JSON-LD context
  "https://w3id.org/dspace/2025/1/context.jsonld"
  on the base path **/api/2025/1**.
  Negotiation and Transfer are **asynchronous**: the receiver
  ACKs immediately (201/200) and later pushes state changes to
  the sender's **callbackAddress**.
end note

== STEP 0: Catalog Discovery (optional sync) ==

Consumer -> Provider: POST /api/2025/1/catalog/request\n[Authorization: Bearer <si_token>]\n[Content-Type: application/json]
note left #FEF9E7
  **CatalogRequestMessage**
  {
    "@context": ["https://w3id.org/dspace/2025/1/context.jsonld"],
    "@type": "CatalogRequestMessage",
    "filter": []
  }
end note
Provider --> Consumer: HTTP 200 OK
note right #EBF5FB
  **Catalog** (dcat:Catalog)
  {
    "@type": "dcat:Catalog",
    "dcat:dataset": [{
      "@id": "urn:uuid:3afeadd8-...-8394a8836d57",
      "odrl:hasPolicy": [{ "@id": "urn:uuid:2828282:...a88", ... }],
      "dcat:distribution": [{
        "dcat:accessService": {
          "dcat:endpointUrl": "http://party-a-connector:3000"
        }
      }]
    }]
  }
end note

== STEP 1: Self-Issued Token Acquisition (DCP handshake) ==

note over Consumer, Provider #FDEDEC
  Performed on demand before each protected DSP call and cached
  until expiry (Authenticator::get_token). The presented token is
  an **ES256** JWT backed by a Verifiable Presentation.
end note

Consumer -> Provider: POST /auth/verify_me\n{ "did_web": "did:web:party-b-connector%3A3000" }
Provider --> Consumer: HTTP 200 OK\n**Session** { session_id, openid4vp_url }

Consumer -> Wallet: POST /wallet/{id}/credentials/present\n{ "request_url": "<openid4vp_url>" }
Wallet --> Provider: OpenID4VP — submit Verifiable Presentation
Wallet --> Consumer: HTTP 200 OK

loop Poll until status == valid (max ~10s, every 3s)
    Consumer -> Provider: GET /auth/status/{session_id}
    Provider --> Consumer: HTTP 200 OK\n**Status** (pending | valid + <access_token>)
end

note over Consumer #EAFAF1
  Consumer now holds a Bearer <si_token> for the Provider.
  (The reverse also happens: when the Provider calls back, it
  first fetches its own token from the Consumer's /auth/verify_me.)
end note

== STEP 2: Contract Negotiation (async, callback-based) ==

Consumer -> Provider: POST /api/2025/1/negotiations/request\n[Authorization: Bearer <si_token>]
note left #FEF9E7
  **ContractRequestMessage**
  {
    "@context": ["https://w3id.org/dspace/2025/1/context.jsonld"],
    "@type": "ContractRequestMessage",
    "consumerPid": "urn:uuid:<consumer_pid>",
    "offer": {
      "@type": "Offer",
      "@id": "urn:uuid:2828282:...a88",
      "target": "urn:uuid:3afeadd8-...-8394a8836d57"
    },
    "callbackAddress": "http://party-b-connector:3000/api/2025/1"
  }
end note

Provider -> Consumer: GET /.well-known/did.json\n(resolve consumer did:web & verify ES256 si_token signature)
Consumer --> Provider: HTTP 200 OK (Consumer DID Document)

Provider --> Consumer: HTTP 201 Created
note right #EBF5FB
  **ContractNegotiation** (state = REQUESTED)
  {
    "@type": "ContractNegotiation",
    "providerPid": "urn:uuid:<provider_pid>",
    "consumerPid": "urn:uuid:<consumer_pid>",
    "state": "REQUESTED"
  }
end note

alt Provider offers a (counter) ContractOffer first
    Provider -> Consumer: POST /api/2025/1/negotiations/{consumer_pid}/offers\n[Authorization: Bearer <provider_si_token>]
    note left #FEF9E7
      **ContractOfferMessage**
      { "@type": "ContractOfferMessage",
        "providerPid": "...", "consumerPid": "...",
        "offer": { "@type": "Offer", ... },
        "callbackAddress": "http://party-a-connector:3000/api/2025/1" }
    end note
    Consumer --> Provider: HTTP 200 OK (state = OFFERED)

    Consumer -> Provider: POST /api/2025/1/negotiations/{provider_pid}/request\n(secondary ContractRequestMessage accepting the offer)
    Provider --> Consumer: HTTP 200 OK (state = ACCEPTED)
else Provider agrees to the consumer's original offer
    note over Provider #EAFAF1: Provider evaluates the offer against its policy engine.
end

== STEP 2b: Agreement & Verification ==

Provider -> Consumer: POST /api/2025/1/negotiations/{consumer_pid}/agreement\n[Authorization: Bearer <provider_si_token>]
note left #EAFAF1
  **ContractAgreementMessage**
  {
    "@type": "ContractAgreementMessage",
    "providerPid": "...", "consumerPid": "...",
    "agreement": {
      "@type": "Agreement",
      "@id": "urn:uuid:<agreement_id>",
      "target": "urn:uuid:3afeadd8-...",
      "assigner": "did:web:party-a-connector%3A3000",
      "assignee": "did:web:party-b-connector%3A3000",
      "timestamp": "2026-08-31T11:06:23Z",
      "permission": [{ "action": "use", "constraint": [...] }]
    }
  }
end note
Consumer --> Provider: HTTP 200 OK (state = AGREED)

Consumer -> Provider: POST /api/2025/1/negotiations/{provider_pid}/agreement/verification\n[Authorization: Bearer <si_token>]
note right #FEF9E7
  **ContractAgreementVerificationMessage**
  { "@type": "ContractAgreementVerificationMessage",
    "providerPid": "...", "consumerPid": "..." }
end note
Provider --> Consumer: HTTP 200 OK (state = VERIFIED)

Provider -> Consumer: POST /api/2025/1/negotiations/{consumer_pid}/events\n[Authorization: Bearer <provider_si_token>]
note left #EBF5FB
  **ContractNegotiationEventMessage**
  { "@type": "ContractNegotiationEventMessage",
    "providerPid": "...", "consumerPid": "...",
    "eventType": "FINALIZED" }
end note
Consumer --> Provider: HTTP 200 OK (state = FINALIZED)

note over Consumer #EAFAF1
  Consumer stores the finalized Agreement.
  GET /api-internal/negotiate/{consumer_pid} now returns
  state "finalized" with the agreement "@id".
end note

== STEP 3: Transfer Process (async, callback-based) ==

Consumer -> Provider: POST /api/2025/1/transfers/request\n[Authorization: Bearer <si_token>]
note left #FEF9E7
  **TransferRequestMessage**
  {
    "@context": ["https://w3id.org/dspace/2025/1/context.jsonld"],
    "@type": "TransferRequestMessage",
    "consumerPid": "urn:uuid:<consumer_pid>",
    "agreementId": "urn:uuid:<agreement_id>",
    "format": "HttpData-PULL",
    "callbackAddress": "http://party-b-connector:3000/api/2025/1"
  }
end note
Provider --> Consumer: HTTP 201 Created
note right #EBF5FB
  **TransferProcess** (state = REQUESTED)
  { "@type": "TransferProcess",
    "providerPid": "...", "consumerPid": "...",
    "state": "REQUESTED" }
end note

Provider -> Consumer: POST /api/2025/1/transfers/{consumer_pid}/start\n[Authorization: Bearer <provider_si_token>]
note left #EAFAF1
  **TransferStartMessage**
  {
    "@type": "TransferStartMessage",
    "providerPid": "...", "consumerPid": "...",
    "dataAddress": {
      "@type": "DataAddress",
      "endpointType": "https://w3id.org/idsa/v4.1/HTTP",
      "endpoint": "http://party-a-connector:3000/pull/...",
      "endpointProperties": [
        { "@type": "EndpointProperty",
          "name": "authorization", "value": "<transfer_token>" }
      ]
    }
  }
end note
Consumer --> Provider: HTTP 200 OK (state = STARTED)

opt Consumer pulls the data (HttpData-PULL)
    Consumer -> Provider: GET/POST http://party-a-connector:3000/pull/...\n[Authorization: <transfer_token>]
    Provider --> Consumer: HTTP 200 OK — dataset payload
    note over Provider #FDEDEC
      Reverse proxy validates the transfer token (new_transfer_token)
      and forwards the request to the backing data source.
    end note
end

Consumer -> Provider: POST /api/2025/1/transfers/{provider_pid}/completion\n[Authorization: Bearer <si_token>]
note right #FEF9E7
  **TransferCompletionMessage**
  { "@type": "TransferCompletionMessage",
    "providerPid": "...", "consumerPid": "..." }
end note
Provider --> Consumer: HTTP 200 OK (state = COMPLETED)

note over Consumer, Provider #EBF5FB
  Either party may also send, at the matching endpoints:
  **TransferSuspensionMessage** (.../{pid}/suspension),
  **TransferTerminationMessage** (.../{pid}/termination),
  or, during negotiation,
  **ContractNegotiationTerminationMessage** (.../{pid}/termination).
end note

@enduml
